IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc3-participation.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II.1 Terrorism, "Participating, Facilitating, Instructing and Harbouring" (ss 83.18 to 83.23)
-- and "Hoax Regarding Terrorist Activity" (s 83.231). Layer 1 (the law, objectively), written by part agent ccc3 from the text alone.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
--
-- READING A RESULT (rule of 2026-10-29): as in `ccc3-interpretation.l4`. Each offence function answers JUST TRUE (every element made out), JUST FALSE (this section does not
-- make the person guilty on these facts; NEVER "not guilty of anything") or NOTHING (the answer turns on a term another section defines and the caller could not say).
-- An unmet element is read as the text's "no" because the sections define each offence by "Every person ... who ..." (fork F-ccc3-1). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Each offence section also gives `the class of the offence` and `the punishment of the offence` (core types): the offences of this range are the ones sections 463 to 465, 515, 553 to 555 and 718.2 ask for.
-- Answers the text borrows are inputs named for the section that gives them: `, by s 83.01(1)` for "terrorist activity" and "terrorist group", `, by s 2 terrorism offence` for "terrorism offence",
-- `, by s 787(1)` for the penalty of an offence "punishable on summary conviction" that states none.
-- "Leaves or attempts to leave Canada, or goes or attempts to go on board a conveyance with the intent to leave Canada" is one plain fact (the four ways are alternatives).

§ `Section 83.18 -- Participation in activity of terrorist group`

-- (1) "knowingly participates in or contributes to, directly or indirectly, any activity of a terrorist group for the purpose of enhancing the ability of any terrorist group to facilitate or carry out a terrorist activity".
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.18(1) the person is guilty of the offence; s 83.18(1) the class of the offence; s 83.18(1) the punishment of the offence | s 83.18(1)
-- src:1639 | Participating, Facilitating, Instructing and Harbouring
-- src:1640 | Participation in activity of terrorist group
-- src:1641 | 83.18 (1) Every person who knowingly participates in or contributes to, directly or indirectly, any activity of a terrorist group for the purpose of enhancing the ability of any terrorist group to facilitate or carry out a terrorist activity is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years.
@ref s 83.18(1) (src:1639-1641)
GIVEN `the person knowingly participates in or contributes to, directly or indirectly, an activity of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of enhancing the ability of any terrorist group to facilitate or carry out a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.18(1) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly participates in or contributes to, directly or indirectly, an activity of the group` AND `it is for the purpose of enhancing the ability of any terrorist group to facilitate or carry out a terrorist activity`
    THEN CONSIDER `the group is a terrorist group, by s 83.01(1)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any activity of a terrorist group"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the group is a terrorist group is for s 83.01(1)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who knowingly participates in or contributes to, directly or indirectly, any activity of a terrorist group"

@ref s 83.18(1) (src:1641)
`s 83.18(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 83.18(1) (src:1641)
`s 83.18(1) the punishment of the offence` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- (2) "An offence may be committed under subsection (1) whether or not (a), (b) or (c)": the three circumstances do not matter. Another circumstance is not covered.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.18(2) the circumstance does not prevent an offence under subsection (1) | s 83.18(2)*
-- src:1642 | Prosecution
-- src:1643 | (2) An offence may be committed under subsection (1) whether or not
-- src:1644 | (a) a terrorist group actually facilitates or carries out a terrorist activity;
-- src:1645 | (b) the participation or contribution of the accused actually enhances the ability of a terrorist group to facilitate or carry out a terrorist activity; or
-- src:1646 | (c) the accused knows the specific nature of any terrorist activity that may be facilitated or carried out by a terrorist group.
@ref s 83.18(2) (src:1642-1646)
DECLARE `s 83.18(2) circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.18(2)(a) a terrorist group actually facilitates or carries out a terrorist activity`
    `s 83.18(2)(b) the participation or contribution of the accused actually enhances the ability of a terrorist group to facilitate or carry out a terrorist activity`
    `s 83.18(2)(c) the accused knows the specific nature of any terrorist activity that may be facilitated or carried out by a terrorist group`
    `s 83.18(2) another circumstance`

@ref s 83.18(2) (src:1642-1646)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 83.18(2) circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.18(2) the circumstance does not prevent an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 83.18(2) another circumstance` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "whether or not"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3) "Participating in or contributing to an activity of a terrorist group includes (a) to (e)": an open list. (c) and (e) turn on "terrorism offence", the answer of section 2.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.18(3) the conduct is participating in or contributing to an activity of a terrorist group | s 83.18(3)*
-- src:1647 | Meaning of participating or contributing
-- src:1648 | (3) Participating in or contributing to an activity of a terrorist group includes
-- src:1649 | (a) providing, receiving or recruiting a person to receive training;
-- src:1650 | (b) providing or offering to provide a skill or an expertise for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group;
-- src:1651 | (c) recruiting a person in order to facilitate or commit
-- src:1652 | (i) a terrorism offence, or
-- src:1653 | (ii) an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be a terrorism offence;
-- src:1654 | (d) entering or remaining in any country for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group; and
-- src:1655 | (e) making oneself, in response to instructions from any of the persons who constitute a terrorist group, available to facilitate or commit
-- src:1656 | (i) a terrorism offence, or
-- src:1657 | (ii) an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be a terrorism offence.
@ref s 83.18(3) (src:1647-1657)
DECLARE `s 83.18(3) conduct` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.18(3)(a) providing, receiving or recruiting a person to receive training`
    `s 83.18(3)(b) providing or offering to provide a skill or an expertise for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group`
    `s 83.18(3)(c)(i) recruiting a person in order to facilitate or commit a terrorism offence`
    `s 83.18(3)(c)(ii) recruiting a person in order to facilitate or commit an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be a terrorism offence`
    `s 83.18(3)(d) entering or remaining in any country for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group`
    `s 83.18(3)(e)(i) making oneself, in response to instructions from any of the persons who constitute a terrorist group, available to facilitate or commit a terrorism offence`
    `s 83.18(3)(e)(ii) making oneself, in response to instructions from any of the persons who constitute a terrorist group, available to facilitate or commit an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be a terrorism offence`
    `s 83.18(3) other conduct`

@ref s 83.18(3) (src:1647-1657)
GIVEN conduct IS A `s 83.18(3) conduct`
      `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.18(3) the conduct is participating in or contributing to an activity of a terrorist group` MEANS
    CONSIDER conduct
    WHEN `s 83.18(3)(a) providing, receiving or recruiting a person to receive training` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.18(3)(b) providing or offering to provide a skill or an expertise for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.18(3)(c)(i) recruiting a person in order to facilitate or commit a terrorism offence` THEN `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
    WHEN `s 83.18(3)(c)(ii) recruiting a person in order to facilitate or commit an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be a terrorism offence` THEN `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
    WHEN `s 83.18(3)(d) entering or remaining in any country for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a terrorist group` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 83.18(3)(e)(i) making oneself, in response to instructions from any of the persons who constitute a terrorist group, available to facilitate or commit a terrorism offence` THEN `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
    WHEN `s 83.18(3)(e)(ii) making oneself, in response to instructions from any of the persons who constitute a terrorist group, available to facilitate or commit an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be a terrorism offence` THEN `the offence is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
    WHEN `s 83.18(3) other conduct` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes"

-- (4) "the court may consider, among other factors, whether the accused (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; or (d) ...".
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.18(4) the court may consider the factor | s 83.18(4)*
-- src:1658 | Factors
-- src:1659 | (4) In determining whether an accused participates in or contributes to any activity of a terrorist group, the court may consider, among other factors, whether the accused
-- src:1660 | (a) uses a name, word, symbol or other representation that identifies, or is associated with, the terrorist group;
-- src:1661 | (b) frequently associates with any of the persons who constitute the terrorist group;
-- src:1662 | (c) receives any benefit from the terrorist group; or
-- src:1663 | (d) repeatedly engages in activities at the instruction of any of the persons who constitute the terrorist group.
@ref s 83.18(4) (src:1658-1663)
DECLARE `s 83.18(4) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 83.18(4)(a) the accused uses a name, word, symbol or other representation that identifies, or is associated with, the terrorist group`
    `s 83.18(4)(b) the accused frequently associates with any of the persons who constitute the terrorist group`
    `s 83.18(4)(c) the accused receives any benefit from the terrorist group`
    `s 83.18(4)(d) the accused repeatedly engages in activities at the instruction of any of the persons who constitute the terrorist group`
    `s 83.18(4) another factor`

@ref s 83.18(4) (src:1658-1663)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 83.18(4) factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.18(4) the court may consider the factor` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 83.18(4) another factor` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may consider, among other factors"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

