-- src:1667 | 83.19 (1) Every one who knowingly facilitates a terrorist activity is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 83.19(1) (src:1666-1667)
GIVEN `the person knowingly facilitates the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is a terrorist activity, by s 83.01(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.19(1) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly facilitates the activity`
    THEN CONSIDER `the activity is a terrorist activity, by s 83.01(1)`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "knowingly facilitates a terrorist activity"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the act is a terrorist activity is for s 83.01(1)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who knowingly facilitates a terrorist activity"

@ref s 83.19(1) (src:1667)
`s 83.19(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 83.19(1) (src:1667)
`s 83.19(1) the punishment of the offence` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- (2) "a terrorist activity is facilitated whether or not (a) the facilitator knows that a particular terrorist activity is facilitated; (b) any particular terrorist activity was foreseen or planned at the time it was facilitated; or (c) any terrorist activity was actually carried out."
-- The three are circumstances that do not matter, so the rule reads none of them (they are asked so that a caller states them, and the answer is the same for every combination: tested).
-- The keel's section 83.01(2) takes this answer as the input `a terrorist activity is facilitated, by s 83.19(2)`.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-18 | s 83.19(2) a terrorist activity is facilitated | s 83.19(2)*
-- src:1668 | Facilitation
-- src:1669 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, a terrorist activity is facilitated whether or not
-- src:1670 | (a) the facilitator knows that a particular terrorist activity is facilitated;
-- src:1671 | (b) any particular terrorist activity was foreseen or planned at the time it was facilitated; or
-- src:1672 | (c) any terrorist activity was actually carried out.
@ref s 83.19(2) (src:1668-1672)
GIVEN `the conduct otherwise facilitates a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the facilitator knows that a particular terrorist activity is facilitated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any particular terrorist activity was foreseen or planned at the time it was facilitated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any terrorist activity was actually carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.19(2) a terrorist activity is facilitated` MEANS
    IF `the conduct otherwise facilitates a terrorist activity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only that the three circumstances do not matter, not what facilitation is

