-- (7) "If the court is not satisfied ..., the court shall order that the electronic copy be returned ... and terminate the order under paragraph (1)(b)."
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-6,F-ccc3-11,F-ccc3-20 | s 83.223(5) the court may order the custodian to delete the material; s 83.223(6) the court may order the destruction of the electronic copy; s 83.223(7) the court must order the copy returned | s 83.223(5); s 83.223(6); s 83.223(7)
-- src:1734 | Order of deletion
-- src:1735 | (5) If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is available to the public and is terrorist propaganda or computer data that makes terrorist propaganda available, it may order the computer system’s custodian to delete the material.
@ref s 83.223(5) (src:1734-1735)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is available to the public and is terrorist propaganda or computer data that makes terrorist propaganda available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.223(5) the court may order the custodian to delete the material` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is available to the public and is terrorist propaganda or computer data that makes terrorist propaganda available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the material is available to the public and is terrorist propaganda"

-- src:1736 | Destruction of electronic copy
-- src:1737 | (6) When the court makes the order for the deletion of the material, it may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court’s possession.
@ref s 83.223(6) (src:1736-1737)
GIVEN `the court makes the order for the deletion of the material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.223(6) the court may order the destruction of the electronic copy` MEANS
    IF `the court makes the order for the deletion of the material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the court makes the order for the deletion of the material, it may order the destruction of the electronic copy in the court’s possession"

-- src:1738 | Return of material
-- src:1739 | (7) If the court is not satisfied that the material is available to the public and is terrorist propaganda or computer data that makes terrorist propaganda available, the court shall order that the electronic copy be returned to the computer system’s custodian and terminate the order under paragraph (1)(b).
@ref s 83.223(7) (src:1738-1739)
GIVEN `the court is not satisfied that the material is available to the public and is terrorist propaganda or computer data that makes terrorist propaganda available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.223(7) the court must order the copy returned` MEANS
    IF `the court is not satisfied that the material is available to the public and is terrorist propaganda or computer data that makes terrorist propaganda available`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court is not satisfied that the material is available to the public and is terrorist propaganda or computer data that makes terrorist propaganda available"

-- (8) the appeal, as 83.222(6) but from an order under (5) or (6); (9) the Attorney General's consent; (10) "No order ... takes effect until the time for final appeal has expired": an "until" bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-16 | s 83.223(8) the person may appeal from the order; s 83.223(9) the proceeding is barred from being instituted; s 83.223(10) the order does not yet take effect | s 83.223(8); s 83.223(9); s 83.223(10)
-- src:1740 | Appeal
-- src:1741 | (8) An appeal lies from an order made under subsection (5) or (6) by any person who appeared before the court, on any ground of appeal that involves a question of law or fact alone, or a question of mixed law and fact, as if it were an appeal against conviction or against a judgment or verdict of acquittal, as the case may be, on a question of law alone under Part XXI, and sections 673 to 696 apply with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 83.223(8) (src:1740-1741)
GIVEN `the order was made under subsection (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appeared before the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of appeal involves a question of law or fact alone, or a question of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.223(8) the person may appeal from the order` MEANS
    IF `the order was made under subsection (5) or (6)` AND `the person appeared before the court` AND `the ground of appeal involves a question of law or fact alone, or a question of mixed law and fact`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal lies from an order made under subsection (5) or (6) by any person who appeared before the court"

-- src:1742 | Consent
-- src:1743 | (9) No proceeding under this section shall be instituted without the Attorney General’s consent.
@ref s 83.223(9) (src:1742-1743)
GIVEN `the Attorney General has consented to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.223(9) the proceeding is barred from being instituted` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General has consented to the proceeding`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceeding under this section shall be instituted without the Attorney General’s consent"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1744 | When order takes effect
-- src:1745 | (10) No order made under any of subsections (5) to (7) takes effect until the time for final appeal has expired.
@ref s 83.223(10) (src:1744-1745)
GIVEN `the order was made under any of subsections (5) to (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time for final appeal has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.223(10) the order does not yet take effect` MEANS
    IF NOT `the order was made under any of subsections (5) to (7)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No order made under any of subsections (5) to (7)"
    ELSE IF `the time for final appeal has expired`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "takes effect until the time for final appeal has expired"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (11): "computer data" and "computer system" have the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2) (part ccc13): answers taken as inputs; "data" is shown repealed;
-- "court", "judge" and "terrorist propaganda" are the terms of subsection 83.222(8) (functions above).
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.223(11) computer data; s 83.223(11) computer system; s 83.222(8) court; s 83.222(8) judge; s 83.222(8) terrorist propaganda | s 83.223(11) "*
-- src:1746 | Definitions
-- src:1747 | (11) The following definitions apply in this section.
-- src:1748 | computer data has the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2). (données informatiques)
-- src:1749 | computer system has the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2). (ordinateur)
-- src:1750 | court has the same meaning as in subsection 320(8). (tribunal)
-- src:1751 | data [Repealed, 2015, c. 20, s. 35]
-- src:1752 | judge has the same meaning as in subsection 320(8). (juge)
-- src:1753 | terrorist propaganda has the same meaning as in subsection 83.222(8). (propagande terroriste)
@ref s 83.223(11) (src:1746-1753)
GIVEN `the thing is computer data, by s 342.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.223(11) computer data` MEANS `the thing is computer data, by s 342.1(2)`

@ref s 83.223(11) (src:1746-1753)
GIVEN `the thing is a computer system, by s 342.1(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.223(11) computer system` MEANS `the thing is a computer system, by s 342.1(2)`

-- 83.23(1): harbouring or concealing a person "whom they know to be a person who has carried out a terrorist activity, for the purpose of enabling that other person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity".
-- (a) 14 years if that person's terrorist activity "is a terrorism offence for which that person is liable to imprisonment for life"; (b) 10 years if "liable to any other punishment".
-- The punishment the other person is liable to is the answer of the offence section (part by part): taken as an input `Punishment`.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.23(1) the person is guilty of the offence; s 83.23(1) the class of the offence; s 83.23(1) the punishment of the offence | s 83.23(1)*
-- src:1754 | Concealing person who carried out terrorist activity
-- src:1755 | 83.23 (1) Every person who knowingly harbours or conceals another person whom they know to be a person who has carried out a terrorist activity, for the purpose of enabling that other person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity, is guilty of
-- src:1756 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years, if the person who is harboured or concealed carried out a terrorist activity that is a terrorism offence for which that person is liable to imprisonment for life; and
-- src:1757 | (b) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years, if the person who is harboured or concealed carried out a terrorist activity that is a terrorism offence for which that person is liable to any other punishment.
@ref s 83.23(1) (src:1754-1757)
GIVEN `the person knowingly harbours or conceals another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the other person has carried out a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of enabling that other person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terrorist activity the other person carried out is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.23(1) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF     `the person knowingly harbours or conceals another person`
       AND `the person knows the other person has carried out a terrorist activity`
       AND `it is for the purpose of enabling that other person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity`
    THEN CONSIDER `the terrorist activity the other person carried out is a terrorism offence, by s 2 terrorism offence`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "carried out a terrorist activity that is a terrorism offence"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the activity is a terrorism offence is for s 2
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who knowingly harbours or conceals another person whom they know to be a person who has carried out a terrorist activity"

@ref s 83.23(1) (src:1755-1757)
`s 83.23(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 83.23(1) (src:1755-1757)
GIVEN `the punishment the terrorism offence is liable to, by the offence section` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 83.23(1) the punishment of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the punishment the terrorism offence is liable to, by the offence section`'s `maximum imprisonment` EQUALS `imprisonment for life`
    THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    ELSE Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- 83.23(2): the person "likely to carry out a terrorist activity": 10 years.
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.23(2) the person is guilty of the offence; s 83.23(2) the class of the offence; s 83.23(2) the punishment of the offence | s 83.23(2)
-- src:1758 | Concealing person who is likely to carry out terrorist activity
-- src:1759 | (2) Every person who knowingly harbours or conceals another person whom they know to be a person who is likely to carry out a terrorist activity, for the purpose of enabling that other person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years.
@ref s 83.23(2) (src:1758-1759)
GIVEN `the person knowingly harbours or conceals another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the other person is likely to carry out a terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of enabling that other person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.23(2) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly harbours or conceals another person` AND `the person knows the other person is likely to carry out a terrorist activity` AND `it is for the purpose of enabling that other person to facilitate or carry out any terrorist activity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who knowingly harbours or conceals another person whom they know to be a person who is likely to carry out a terrorist activity"

@ref s 83.23(2) (src:1759)
`s 83.23(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 83.23(2) (src:1759)
`s 83.23(2) the punishment of the offence` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 83.231 -- Hoax: terrorist activity`

-- (1) "Every one commits an offence who, without lawful excuse and with intent to cause any person to fear death, bodily harm, substantial damage to property or serious interference with the lawful use or operation of property,
-- (a) conveys or causes or procures to be conveyed information that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur, without believing the information to be true; or
-- (b) commits an act that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension ..., without believing that such activity is occurring or will occur."
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.231(1) the person commits the offence | s 83.231(1)*
-- src:1761 | Hoax Regarding Terrorist Activity
-- src:1762 | Hoax — terrorist activity
-- src:1763 | 83.231 (1) Every one commits an offence who, without lawful excuse and with intent to cause any person to fear death, bodily harm, substantial damage to property or serious interference with the lawful use or operation of property,
-- src:1764 | (a) conveys or causes or procures to be conveyed information that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur, without believing the information to be true; or
-- src:1765 | (b) commits an act that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur, without believing that such activity is occurring or will occur.
@ref s 83.231(1) (src:1761-1765)
DECLARE `s 83.231(1) facts` HAS
    `the person has a lawful excuse`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person intends to cause a person to fear death, bodily harm, substantial damage to property or serious interference with the lawful use or operation of property`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person conveys, or causes or procures to be conveyed, information that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `the person believes the information to be true`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `the person commits an act that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `the person believes that such activity is occurring or will occur`                                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)

@ref s 83.231(1) (src:1761-1765)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 83.231(1) facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.231(1) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF     (NOT facts's `the person has a lawful excuse`)
       AND facts's `the person intends to cause a person to fear death, bodily harm, substantial damage to property or serious interference with the lawful use or operation of property`
       AND (    (facts's `the person conveys, or causes or procures to be conveyed, information that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur` AND (NOT facts's `the person believes the information to be true`))
             OR (facts's `the person commits an act that, in all the circumstances, is likely to cause a reasonable apprehension that terrorist activity is occurring or will occur` AND (NOT facts's `the person believes that such activity is occurring or will occur`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one commits an offence who, without lawful excuse and with intent to cause any person to fear death"

-- (2) "(a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction": (b) states no penalty, so the general penalty of section 787(1) is an input.
-- COVERS: encoded | s 83.231(2) the class of the offence; s 83.231(2) the punishments of the offence | s 83.231(2)*
-- src:1766 | Punishment
-- src:1767 | (2) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:1768 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:1769 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 83.231(2) (src:1766-1769)
`s 83.231(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 83.231(2) (src:1766-1769)
GIVEN `the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction, by s 787(1)` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 83.231(2) the punishments of the offence` MEANS
    LIST
        (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`),
        `the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction, by s 787(1)`

-- (3) "Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) and thereby causes bodily harm to any other person is guilty of (a) an indictable offence ... not exceeding ten years; or (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction."
-- "bodily harm" is the answer of section 2 (the keel's `s 2 bodily harm`).
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.231(3) the person commits the offence causing bodily harm; s 83.231(3) the class of the offence; s 83.231(3) the punishments of the offence | s 83.231(3)*
-- src:1770 | Causing bodily harm
-- src:1771 | (3) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) and thereby causes bodily harm to any other person is guilty of
-- src:1772 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:1773 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 83.231(3) (src:1770-1773)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection (1), by s 83.231(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person thereby causes bodily harm to any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that harm is bodily harm, by s 2 bodily harm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83.231(3) the person commits the offence causing bodily harm` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person commits an offence under subsection (1), by s 83.231(1)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) and thereby causes bodily harm to any other person"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person commits an offence under subsection (1) is for that subsection
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person thereby causes bodily harm to any other person`
        THEN `that harm is bodily harm, by s 2 bodily harm`
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and thereby causes bodily harm to any other person"

@ref s 83.231(3) (src:1770-1773)
`s 83.231(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 83.231(3) (src:1770-1773)
GIVEN `the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction, by s 787(1)` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 83.231(3) the punishments of the offence` MEANS
    LIST
        (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`),
        `the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction, by s 787(1)`

-- (4) "Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) and thereby causes the death of any other person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life."
-- COVERS: fork F-ccc3-1 | s 83.231(4) the person commits the offence causing death; s 83.231(4) the class of the offence; s 83.231(4) the punishment of the offence | s 83.231(4)
-- src:1774 | Causing death
-- src:1775 | (4) Every one who commits an offence under subsection (1) and thereby causes the death of any other person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
